---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Mexican-Owned LGBTQIA+ Travel Experiences in Tulum | Queerness Experiences" description={"Mexican-owned and operated LGBT and LGBTQIA+ travel experiences in Tulum. Tours and group trips for lesbian, gay, bi, trans, and queer travelers, queer families, and queer destination weddings. Led by Santi Solís, UCLA wildlife biologist and local queer guide."}>

<!-- HERO — dominant H1, then photo, then body, then CTAs -->
<header class="hero">
  <div class="shape-y"></div>
  <div class="shape-t"></div>
  <p class="hero-eye">★ Mexican-Owned &amp; Operated · LGBTQIA+ Travel Experiences in Latin America</p>
  <h1>
    <span class="l l1">Tours &amp; group trips</span>
    <span class="l l2">for queer &amp; trans</span>
    <span class="l l3">people in</span>
    <span class="l l4">Tulum.</span>
  </h1>
  <div class="hero-photo-wrap">
    <div class="ph ph-light hero-photo">PHOTO — SANTI · TULUM · CANDID</div>
    <div class="hero-photo-tag">Santi · Founder</div>
  </div>
  <p class="hero-body">I create travel experiences in Tulum, Mexico, to introduce travelers to the people and places that make it so special. <strong>I'm Santi (they/them)</strong>. Born in Mexico, raised in the U.S., former UCLA wildlife biologist, and conference speaker on creating queer experiences.</p>
  <div class="cta-stack">
    <a href="#tours" class="btn-p">See the Tours →</a>
    <a href="/group-trips" class="btn-s">Upcoming Group Trips →</a>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- QUEER-FRIENDLY BAR — under hero -->
<section style="background:var(--yellow);border-bottom:6px solid var(--blue);padding:20px var(--s-sm);">
  <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--dark);line-height:1.6;font-weight:500;max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center;">Tulum being queer and trans friendly surprises people. It's not a queer-centric town, but you'll see queer and gender-diverse people any time you walk out on the street. We're a regular part of the community and of daily life here.</p>
  <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--dark);line-height:1.6;max-width:640px;margin:10px auto 0;text-align:center;">Most hotels and destinations here are already this welcoming, they just don't know how to express it, which is part of why they never get tagged as a queer or LGBTQ+ focused destination. I help with that. <a href="/work-with-me" style="color:var(--blue);font-weight:700;text-decoration:underline;">See how we could work together →</a></p>
</section>

<!-- SOCIAL PROOF STRIP -->
<a href="#reviews" style="text-decoration:none;display:block;">
<section style="background:var(--white);border-bottom:3px solid var(--dark);padding:18px var(--s-sm);cursor:pointer;transition:background 0.15s;">
  <div style="max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;text-align:center;">
    <span style="color:var(--yellow);font-size:18px;letter-spacing:2px;">★★★★★</span>
    <span style="font-family:var(--fb);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;color:var(--dark);">19 five-star reviews on Google</span>
    <span style="font-family:var(--fb);font-size:13px;color:var(--magenta);font-weight:700;">Read them →</span>
  </div>
</section>
</a>

<!-- PHOTO BAND — real queer joy in Tulum -->
<section style="background:var(--bone);border-bottom:3px solid var(--dark);padding:0;">
  <div class="photo-band">
    <div class="pb-img">PHOTO — QUEER JOY (real moment, tour, laughter)</div>
    <div class="pb-img">PHOTO — TULUM NATURE (cenote / jungle)</div>
    <div class="pb-img">PHOTO — FOOD / CULTURE</div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- BRIDGE + CREDENTIALS -->
<section class="bridge">
  <p>Born in Mexico. Raised in the U.S. Came home to build a life in Tulum.</p>
  <p class="folx">Recently cast as a model for a campaign by FOLX, the queer and trans telehealth company.</p>
  <p class="small">A bit about me</p>
</section>
<section class="creds" aria-label="Credentials">
  <div class="cred"><div class="cnum">01</div><div><div class="ct">UCLA Wildlife Biologist</div><div class="cd">The science behind every tour you take with me.</div></div></div>
  <div class="cred"><div class="cnum">02</div><div><div class="ct">Pattie Gonia Scholarship</div><div class="cd">Queer Outdoor Expedition recipient, 2023.</div></div></div>
  <div class="cred"><div class="cnum">03</div><div><div class="ct">International Conference Speaker</div><div class="cd">On designing experiences for queer travelers.</div></div></div>
  <div class="cred"><div class="cnum">04</div><div><div class="ct">Co-Host · Group Trips &amp; Retreats</div><div class="cd">In collaboration with Queer Connect.</div></div></div>
</section>

<!-- GUIDE — above tours -->
<section class="guide" id="guide">
  <div class="guide-inner">
    <p class="sec-eye" style="color:var(--yellow);">Free Tulum recommendations</p>
    <h2>Stop planning.<br><span class="accent">Start enjoying.</span></h2>
    <p class="guide-lead">My real recommendations for when you visit, free.</p>
    <div class="guide-photo">PHOTO — TULUM FOOD / COFFEE / STREET SCENE (warm, real, makes them want to be here)</div>
    <div class="guide-box">
      <ul class="ginc">
        <li>My favorite coffee shop, restaurant, and a queer-friendly bar</li>
        <li>No Uber in Tulum: here's the taxi app locals use for the best prices</li>
        <li>ATMs are set up to charge you on the conversion. Here's the way around it.</li>
      </ul>
      <a href="/blog/queer-tulum-recommendations" class="btn-p" style="text-align:center;">Get the Free Recommendations →</a>
      <div class="gstat">Book any tour and the full guidebook is yours free.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- TOURS — two flagships + mini boxes -->
<section class="tours" id="tours">
  <div class="tours-inner">
    <p class="sec-eye">What we do</p>
    <h2>The tours</h2>
    <p class="tours-lead">Tours run small, no more than four people. Bigger group, retreat, or event? That becomes a private tour, sized and priced for your group.</p>

    <div class="flagship-row">
      <div class="flagship">
        <div class="ph">PHOTO — SECRET CENOTE</div>
        <div class="flag-tag">Most booked</div>
        <div class="flag-body">
          <div class="flag-name">Secret Cenote</div>
          <p class="flag-desc">A cenote the ancient Maya built that almost nobody knows exists. You enter through a well, into water that's been here for thousands of years. Run by a local Maya family who genuinely loves this place.</p>
          <div class="flag-foot">
            <span class="flag-price">FROM 2,200 MXN / PERSON</span>
            <a href="/book" class="flag-link">BOOK →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flagship">
        <div class="ph">PHOTO — MUYIL RIVER</div>
        <div class="flag-tag">A local favorite</div>
        <div class="flag-body">
          <div class="flag-name">Muyil River Float</div>
          <p class="flag-desc">Float through canals the ancient Maya carved through the jungle. Lagoons, mangroves, open sky. The most relaxing day in Tulum, and the one people keep talking about when they get home.</p>
          <div class="flag-foot">
            <span class="flag-price">FROM 3,400 MXN / PERSON</span>
            <a href="/book" class="flag-link">BOOK →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flagship-row flagship-row-3">
      <div class="flagship">
        <div class="ph">PHOTO — STORIES BEHIND THE STOREFRONT</div>
        <div class="flag-body">
          <div class="flag-name">Stories Behind the Storefront</div>
          <p class="flag-desc">Find out what it's like to live in Tulum. Local shops, murals, and the real Tulum behind the tourist version, the town behind the town.</p>
          <div class="flag-foot">
            <span class="flag-price">FROM 2,400 MXN / PERSON</span>
            <a href="/book" class="flag-link">BOOK →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flagship">
        <div class="ph">PHOTO — STREET FOOD</div>
        <div class="flag-body">
          <div class="flag-name">Street Food</div>
          <p class="flag-desc">Tacos, tostilocos, and elotes at the food trucks locals actually eat at. The guidebooks haven't found these spots yet. Food and drinks included.</p>
          <div class="flag-foot">
            <span class="flag-price">FROM 2,000 MXN / PERSON</span>
            <a href="/book" class="flag-link">BOOK →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flagship">
        <div class="ph">PHOTO — MONKEY SPOTTING</div>
        <div class="flag-body">
          <div class="flag-name">Monkey Spotting + Lagoon Jungle Adventure</div>
          <p class="flag-desc">Wild spider monkeys, zip lining, canoeing, and a swim in a pristine lagoon. Led by a UCLA wildlife biologist, so you actually understand what you're looking at.</p>
          <div class="flag-foot">
            <span class="flag-price">FROM 4,000 MXN / PERSON</span>
            <a href="/book" class="flag-link">BOOK →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tours-all">
      <a href="/tours" class="btn-alltours">See the Tours →</a>
      <a href="/group-trips" class="btn-alltours" style="box-shadow:5px 5px 0 var(--magenta);margin-top:16px;">Group Trips &amp; Retreats →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- GROUP TRIPS COMING UP -->
<section class="groups" id="groups">
  <p class="sec-eye">Coming up</p>
  <h2>Group trips<br>coming up</h2>
  <p>I'm hosting queer group trips in Tulum and beyond. A group trip with Queer Connect, plus two new experiences of my own on the way: the Luxury Lesbians retreat, a lesbian-focused escape for queer and trans professionals 30+, and Camp Queerness.</p>
  <a href="/group-trips" class="btn-groups">See Upcoming Group Trips →</a>
</section>

<!-- FRIEND -->
<section class="friend">
  <p class="sec-eye">Not booking a tour?</p>
  <h2>Looking for a<br>queer friend?</h2>
  <p>I do a lot of activities. You're welcome to join.</p>
  <p class="hobbies">Dance class · jiu jitsu · life drawing night · theatre in Spanish · and whatever else is happening that week.</p>
  <a href="/book" class="btn-friend" style="display:inline-block;text-decoration:none;text-align:center;">Tell me what you're up to →</a>
</section>


<!-- REVIEWS -->
<section class="reviews" id="reviews">
  <p class="sec-eye" style="color:var(--yellow);">Real reviews</p>
  <h2>What queer &amp; trans<br>travelers say</h2>
  <div class="review-scroll">
    <div class="rcard">
      <div class="rstars">★★★★★</div>
      <input type="checkbox" id="rev1" class="rev-toggle">
      <p class="rtext">[ Paste your best Google review here, the one that names a specific tour and a specific moment. If it's long, that's fine, the "read more" will handle it and let people keep reading without making the card huge. ]</p>
      <label for="rev1" class="rev-more">Read more +</label>
      <p class="rname">— [Name], [tour]</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rcard">
      <div class="rstars">★★★★★</div>
      <input type="checkbox" id="rev2" class="rev-toggle">
      <p class="rtext">[ A review from a couple or honeymoon, mentioning how they felt. Paste the full thing here even if it's long. ]</p>
      <label for="rev2" class="rev-more">Read more +</label>
      <p class="rname">— [Name], [tour]</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rcard">
      <div class="rstars">★★★★★</div>
      <input type="checkbox" id="rev3" class="rev-toggle">
      <p class="rtext">[ A review that mentions Santi by name and the local knowledge. ]</p>
      <label for="rev3" class="rev-more">Read more +</label>
      <p class="rname">— [Name], [tour]</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rcard">
      <div class="rstars">★★★★★</div>
      <input type="checkbox" id="rev4" class="rev-toggle">
      <p class="rtext">[ A fourth review — swipe to see more. ]</p>
      <label for="rev4" class="rev-more">Read more +</label>
      <p class="rname">— [Name], [tour]</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="scroll-hint">← Swipe to read more reviews →</p>
  <a href="#" class="btn-reviews">Read all 19 reviews on Google →</a>
</section>

<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="faq" id="faq">
  <p class="sec-eye">Before you book</p>
  <h2>Questions queer &amp;<br>trans travelers ask</h2>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <div class="faq-item">
      <input type="checkbox" id="faq1" checked>
      <label class="faq-q" for="faq1">Is Tulum safe for queer and trans travelers?<span class="tog">+</span></label>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Tulum is one of the most welcoming places in Mexico for queer and trans visitors. I wrote a full, honest guide on what to expect. <a href="/blog/is-tulum-safe-for-queer-trans-travelers">Read: Is Tulum Safe for Queer &amp; Trans Travelers?</a></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <input type="checkbox" id="faq2">
      <label class="faq-q" for="faq2">Is Tulum queer and trans friendly?<span class="tog">+</span></label>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Yes, with real nuance worth understanding before you arrive. Here's the honest version. <a href="/blog/is-tulum-queer-trans-friendly">Read: Is Tulum Queer &amp; Trans Friendly?</a></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <input type="checkbox" id="faq3">
      <label class="faq-q" for="faq3">How big are the tour groups?<span class="tog">+</span></label>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Tours run small, no more than four people, so you're never in a crowd. Larger groups, retreats, and events become private tours, sized and priced for your group.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <input type="checkbox" id="faq4">
      <label class="faq-q" for="faq4">Do I need to book in advance?<span class="tog">+</span></label>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Ideally, yes. About a week's notice is great, especially December through March. But if it's short notice, just message me and I'll do my best to make it work.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CONTACT -->
<section class="contact" id="contact">
  <p class="sec-eye">Book a tour</p>
  <h2>When are you<br>arriving?</h2>
  <p class="contact-lead">Tell me your dates and which tour interests you. I'll reply within 24 hours.</p>
  <a href="/book" class="btn-p" style="display:inline-block;text-align:center;">Book Your Tour in Tulum →</a>
</section>

<!-- FOOTER -->

</Layout>

